From 5bcf6f356de39d6c2738fa43498bb6b11d918261 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aaron <aaronmedeiros@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 22 Aug 2026 16:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] sub: add fitted rounded background boxes

---
 DOCS/man/options.rst |  12 +++++
 options/options.c    |   5 ++
 options/options.h    |   2 +
 sub/sd_ass.c         | 137 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 156 insertions(+)

diff --git a/DOCS/man/options.rst b/DOCS/man/options.rst
index c83c979f7..1e7b19a31 100644
--- a/DOCS/man/options.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/options.rst
@@ -2664,6 +2664,18 @@ Subtitles
 ``--sub-line-spacing=<value>``
     Set line spacing value for SSA/ASS renderer.
 
+``--sub-background-box-padding=<-1..1000>``
+    Replace a text subtitle's ``background-box`` with a box fitted to its
+    rendered glyph bounds and add this many 720p-scaled pixels of padding.
+    ``-1`` (the default) preserves libass' native font-metric box exactly.
+    Authored ASS subtitles are affected only when the user's background-box
+    style is being applied; bitmap subtitles are unaffected.
+
+``--sub-background-box-radius=<0..1000>``
+    Round fitted background-box corners by this many 720p-scaled pixels.
+    This option has an effect only when ``--sub-background-box-padding`` is
+    non-negative. The default is ``0`` (square corners).
+
 ``--sub-shaper=<simple|complex>``
     Set the text layout engine used by libass.
 
